  "reasoning_content": "We need respond to user: \"Write a detailed tutorial on implementing a bounded LRU cache in Python using collections.OrderedDict. Include a complete class, explain get and put behavior, discuss edge cases, and include tests. Continue with a worked example and complexity analysis. Be precise and use meaningful prose and code.\"\n\nNeed produce final tutorial. Need think thoroughly. Need include code complete class, tests, worked example, complexity. Use collections.OrderedDict. Need precise. Could include Python 3.7+ dict ordered? But specifically OrderedDict. Need likely Python 3.8. Need explain get: if key missing return default, move_to_end if hit. put: if existing update and move_to_end, if new and over capacity evict least recently used (popitem(last=False)). Capacity validation. Edge cases: capacity <=0? Could raise ValueError. get default. put value arbitrary. Keys hashable. Concurrency not thread-safe. OrderedDict methods: move_to_end(key, last=True), popitem(last=True/False), pop(key), del. Behavior details: when updating existing, should it move to most recently used? Typically yes for LRU. Could discuss alternative but implement standard.\n\nNeed include tests using unittest or pytest. Could include both? Provide complete class and tests. Need maybe show doctest? Let's design.\n\nClass LRUCache:\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"Bounded least recently used cache.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int) -> None:\n        if capacity < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"capacity must be positive\")\n        self._capacity = capacity\n        self._cache: OrderedDict[int, T] = OrderedDict()\nMaybe type variables. Use Generic? Could be overkill. Simpler.\n\n    def get(self, key: K, default: Optional[T] = None) -> Optional[T]:\n        if key not in self._cache:\n            return default\n        self._cache.move_to_end(key)\n        return self._cache[key]\n\n    def put(self, key: K, value: T) -> None:\n        if key in self._cache:\n            self._cache[key] = value\n            self._cache.move_to_end(key)\n            return\n        if len(self._cache) >= self._capacity:\n            self._cache.popitem(last=False)\n        self._cache[key] = value\n\n    def __len__(self): return len",
